[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4558025898","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119824#issuecomment-4558025898","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119824","id":4558025898,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABD630qg","user":{"login":"fakemaxwell","id":59422275,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5NDIyMjc1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/59422275?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fakemaxwell","html_url":"https://github.com/fakemaxwell","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fakemaxwell/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fakemaxwell/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fakemaxwell/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fakemaxwell/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fakemaxwell/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fakemaxwell/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fakemaxwell/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fakemaxwell/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fakemaxwell/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-27T19:35:18Z","updated_at":"2026-05-27T19:35:18Z","body":"Oh boy- I was playing around with different shapes to see if anything improved the response.  Instead I got this wacky interaction:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3f78367c-1a8d-4dac-a606-85fc08530e4c\n\nOrange is CharacterBody2D, the boxes are RigidBody2Ds.  The CB never reports a collision with any RigidBody, even while being rolled around by them.  ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4558025898/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4569135445","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119824#issuecomment-4569135445","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119824","id":4569135445,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABEFd5VQ","user":{"login":"Schnorg","id":44937651,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0OTM3NjUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44937651?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg","html_url":"https://github.com/Schnorg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-28T23:23:39Z","updated_at":"2026-05-28T23:25:27Z","body":"I ran your sample, and just wanted to note that if you drop the physics frame rate of your sample to 10 FPS, then everything will visibly interpenetrate and you still won't get a rigid collision report.\n\nI also tried your sample with rapier (at 10FPS) and the capsule was then pushed through the ground. \n\nJust sharing in case these are clues for a CharacterBody2D expert.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4569135445/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4573855353","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119824#issuecomment-4573855353","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119824","id":4573855353,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABEJ9-eQ","user":{"login":"Schnorg","id":44937651,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0OTM3NjUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44937651?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg","html_url":"https://github.com/Schnorg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-29T10:24:50Z","updated_at":"2026-05-29T10:24:50Z","body":"I am fairly certain, after looking through the code and docs, that move_and_slide() will only return collisions that changed the motion of the character body as it moved along its path. It won't return every collision it finds, only the ones relevant to its movement.\n\nSo I believe that this is working as intended\n\nAdding Area2D children to your body nodes can be a more reliable (and faster) way to detect game rule collisions. \n\nIn addition to using Area2D for collision detection, you could try to minimize the collision_mask flags in your CharacterBody2D and make it only respond to world and platform-like geometry. \n\nYou can still have rigid bodies collide with the character, by having the rigid body mask flags set to detect the player (while not the other way around). Then when rigid bodies collide with the player, the player will act like an infinite mass from their perspective (I believe). \n\nIf, conversely, the character body mask flags are set to detect the rigid body, then those rigid bodies will act like immovable floors / walls / ceilings to the player, and if you crush the player between them, then the behaviour of move_and_collide() may become a bit undefined (and vary between different physics engines or settings).\n\nSo either make sure you aren't crushing the player, or make the player a rigid body so that it can push back and stack with all the other rigid bodies (but then you lose a lot of the easy to use platformer behaviour of the character body).\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4573855353/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5311310676","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119824#issuecomment-5311310676","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119824","id":5311310676,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABPJQrVA","user":{"login":"themirman","id":80926754,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwOTI2NzU0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/80926754?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/themirman","html_url":"https://github.com/themirman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/themirman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/themirman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/themirman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/themirman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/themirman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/themirman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/themirman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/themirman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/themirman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-17T03:07:23Z","updated_at":"2026-08-17T03:07:23Z","body":"I found that setting the friction of the rigid body to 0 stops it from pushing the character body into the ground when dropped from above. not sure if that helps at all. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5311310676/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]